NAME
    tail - output the last lines of input or a file

SYNOPSIS
    tail [-n N] [path]

DESCRIPTION
    Prints the last N lines (default 10) of piped standard input, or of
    [path] inside the shell sandbox when no standard input is piped.
    Follow mode (-f) is not supported.

OPTIONS
    -n N
        Number of trailing lines to print (non-negative integer, default
        10).

EXAMPLES
    history | tail -n 5
    tail /Logs/run.log
    tail -n 20 /Logs/notes.txt

EXIT STATUS
    0   Lines printed.
    1   Invalid -n value, missing input and path, path outside sandbox,
        or file not found.

SEE ALSO
    head(1), cat(1), wc(1)
